whose presented group is non-trivial: Todd-Coxeter gives order 120 for the 84 rows marked
A5 (a perfect group of order 120 is SL(2,5)), and more than 20,000 cosets for the 28 rows
marked PSL27, whose group surjects onto PSL(2,7).  Each block carries an explicit pair of
permutations killing both relators and not both trivial; the kernel checks both the
relator condition (`_rel`, a `decide` on a permutation equation) and, through the
campaign's bridge `not_acEquiv_standard_of_witness` of `ACQuot.lean`, that the
presentation is not AC-equivalent to the standard pair.
